{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"balladic-rutile-oyster","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n17 modules under `tests/interfaces/` (16 pairs: 1 in `contracts/`, 6 in `facades/`, 6 in `lifecycle/`, 1 in `store/`, 2 at the directory root) and `tests/integration/` (1 pair, `test_s3_doctor.py`) have a `<name>_heldout.py` twin. Once both oracles have been reviewed the split only doubles module count, duplicates identical helper definitions, and makes every rename touch two files. Across these 17 pairs no test-function name collides; 5 pairs carry helper definitions with differing bodies and every other colliding definition is identical. The pair list with per-pair rename sets, filtered from enumeration (2) of the test-suite epic's first comment, is itemised in this ticket's first comment. Cites are on origin/main 083620b0.\n\n## Approach\nDirectories: `tests/interfaces/` and `tests/integration/` — 17 pairs, 5 renames (`test_bridge_status`, `test_detected_by`, `test_ac_checkbox_precheck`, `test_close_gate_subtree`, `test_metrics_cli`). For each pair: `cat` the held-out module into the base under a `# ── held-out oracles (merged from <name>_heldout.py) ──` divider; keep the base module docstring and append the held-out docstring's \"what it proves\" paragraph; dedupe identical definitions (`pytestmark` counts here — keep the base copy); rename differing definitions and repoint their callers; `git rm` the held-out file. Rename rule: suffix the HELD-OUT definition `_heldout` (e.g. `_load_heldout`) and repoint its callers; keep the base copy of identical definitions. `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_gate_subtree.py` cites bug ferric-jet-scorpion in its docstring; that docstring stays the base docstring. No test body changes.\n\n## Scope\nIn scope: the 17 base modules under `tests/interfaces/` and `tests/integration/` named in the first comment and their 17 `_heldout` twins. Out of scope: the `tests/unit/` pairs (S1, S2), `tests/scripts/` (S4), the 78 unpaired held-out renames (S5) — including `tests/interfaces/facades/test_reconciler_last_pass_heldout.py` and `tests/interfaces/store/test_repair_pause_ownership_heldout.py`, which have no base twin in this directory — every file under `src/`, and any test body change.\n\n## Testing\nPer pair: `pytest --collect-only -q <base> <heldout>` before and `pytest --collect-only -q <base>` after — counts equal (both recorded on this ticket); `pytest <base>` green (the `tests/integration/test_s3_doctor.py` pair runs under `-m integration`). `make test` green.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Zero paired twins remain in these directories: for each of the 17 pairs `git ls-files <base>_heldout.py` prints nothing (the unpaired `_heldout` modules in these directories are untouched here and renamed in S5).\n- [ ] Per-pair node counts reconcile: each merged base collects exactly the sum of the two prior counts, from the before/after `pytest --collect-only -q` runs recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` shows `new=0` (no autouse fixture lives in these pairs).\n- [ ] `make verify` green.","id":"fb5f-54fd-96cc-4105","parent_id":"6ed2-24e5-6985-4faa","priority":2,"tags":["complexity-reduction","breaking-pass-4"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Merge the 17 held-out twin test pairs under tests/interfaces and tests/integration"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788807278200952377,"uuid":"d168d702-503e-4f5d-bbbf-515dddc27e10"}